codex
The native-list predicate still leaves “impossible” non-integer branches opaque to this backend. I’m switching back to a constructor-level symbolic grid and changing the specification folds to accumulator form. That preserves integer types by construction and makes each induction step syntactically identical, avoiding both impossible sort branches and arithmetic reassociation obligations.
apply patch
